Note a small to-do list manager end note.
Make a list called tasks.
Set running to yes.
Say text Commands, add a task by typing it, or type show, done, or quit. end text
While running is equal to yes,
  Ask the user for command.
  If command is equal to text show end text, then
    If the length of tasks is equal to 0, then
      Say text Nothing to do. end text
    end if.
    Count from 1 to the length of tasks using i,
      Say i, text -- end text, item i of tasks.
    end loop.
  otherwise if command is equal to text quit end text, then
    Set running to no.
  otherwise if command is equal to text done end text, then
    Say text Which one is finished? Type its number. end text
    Ask the user for a number called which one.
    Remove item which one from tasks.
    Say text Nice, that is done. end text
  otherwise
    Add command to tasks.
    Say text Added. end text
  end if.
end loop.
Say text Bye! end text.
